## Commit conventions

Follow **Conventional Commits**:

- `feat(scope): ...` — new feature.
- `fix(scope): ...` — bug fix.
- `refactor(scope): ...` — code change that neither fixes a bug nor
  adds a feature.
- `chore(scope): ...` — maintenance (dependencies, tooling, cleanup).
- `docs(scope): ...` — documentation only.
- `test(scope): ...` — adding or refactoring tests.
- `perf(scope): ...` — performance improvement.

### Structure

- A short title line, imperative mood, no trailing period, ≤ 72
  characters.
- A blank line.
- A detailed body explaining **what** changed and **why**. Include
  design decisions and their rationale. If a behavior was dropped or
  changed, explain why.

### Delivery format

The assistant delivers the commit as a **single fenced code block**
ready to copy and paste into `git commit`. No surrounding prose
inside the block.

